              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सान्निध्यम् (sānnidhyam) is built on saṃnidhi, \"nearness\", from sam, ni and the root √dhā, \"to put\", with the lengthening of its first vowel; MW gives \"the being near, nearness, vicinity, presence\" (MW)."
